            <div xml:id="d119">

                <pb facs="0160" n="86" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg86"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/5197</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-07T20:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 7, 1917, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 8, 1.15 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6391. Your 4942, June 6, 6 p.m. Northcliffe is sent on a purely commercial errand to supervise
                    the purchasing agents of the British Government in the United States. He has no
                    diplomatic errand or standing nor is he a “commissioner or commissioner general”
                    nor do his duties have any reference to what Mr. Balfour did.</p>
                <p>He knows the United States better than any Englishman except Bryce and he will
                    have no official relations with our Government different from the British
                    commercial agents now there.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
